      "role": "user",
      "content": "that fork in the road metaphor is helpful. so it's basically like a roadblock that's sitting right in the middle of the path. \n\ncan you expand on that? if lisinopril is just sitting there occupying that space, what happens specifically when the angiotensin I molecules arrive? do they just bounce off, or is there something about the way the drug \"occupies\" the site that makes it especially hard for the enzyme to just ignore it and move on? i'm trying to understand the \"strength\" of that blockade.",
      "source": "evaluator"
